// Bundles shown in the in-game gem shop ("Purchase Gems"). Handled by Acts/Act_Billing.cs.
//
// Nothing here costs real money - the Steam payment path is bypassed - so "price" / "currency"
// are inert and only exist because the client requires the fields. "f_price" is the string the
// store button displays.
//
// [WARNING] Every product must define the full set of keys below. The client parses the product
// list as a unit, so a single product missing a key (even one it never displays) fails the whole
// screen with "Failed to load product information". Blank the values instead of deleting keys.
//
// Field notes:
//   product_id    identifier echoed back in the billing ticket. Never validated.
//   items         { "<itemId>": <amount> }. 1 = Gem, 2 = GemAlt. YgoMaster keeps a single gem
//                 pool so both are summed - use "1" unless you want the paid/free split shown
//                 on the tile.
//   string_id     text id for the product name. The displayed name includes the gem total, so
//                 it updates automatically when "items" changes.
//   thumb_id      which gem pile / box artwork the tile uses (1-7).
//   style         0 = normal tile, 1 = featured tile.
//   limit_count   max purchases, -1 for unlimited. buy_count is how many have been made.
//                 [NOTE] buy_count is only tracked in the response, so limits reset when the
//                 server restarts. See the TODO in Act_Billing.cs.
//   sort          display order.
